"***** The Demise of Osama bin Laden *****": [
"Userscen/Demise of Osma READ ME .txt"
],
"- this scenario is now fully compatible with PeG Equipment file v2.7, and also uses lots of new units, not avaible in the previous version of the equipment file; some modfications and better balancing have also been made. German units and Italian units now approach the stronghold from different directions (because now Italian troops are well balanced and don't need anymore \"foreign support\" to be higly effective). Obviously, it's still a good strategy manage to make Italian troops coming as soon as possible to aid German troops, since the stronghold it's, surprisingly enough, really hard to take :)": [
"Userscen/RetStal27_README.txt"
],
"4 Player (Mulitplayer recommended)": [
"Scenario/SEOUL4MP.TXT"
],
"Ah, to take advantage of German equipment.  Purchased another Leopard 2A5 and an older Leopard 1A4, for a total of five tank units.  I also added an Ocelot, since I have a nagging feeling that I don't have enough AD, the Eurosam aside.  So my AD and air units are basically French, tanks are German and British, and most of my infantry are German.  Recons are a mixed bag.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"Although the enemy was properly equipped, once again your skills were too much for them.  For now our supply lines through the jungle will remain.": [
"Scenario/NVC03_bv.TXT"
],
"An agreement took place by which China and Russia agree not to intervene in the conflict anymore and to let UN troops launching police operations in Bangladesh to ensure the smooth return to democracy with the legitimate leaders in place before the coup.": [
"Scenario/IND4bv.TXT"
],
"Anyway, this is another of those scenarios that is always a bit more intimidating than fun.  Lose a few core units and face lots of tough infantry that can't be ferreted out with heavy artillery.  The GCT did its best with devastating fire used to good effect.  The AVLB came in handy as well when it came time to cross the Volga.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"At least we secured Vietnam but the hope to get soon rid of the rebellion leaders is gone!": [
"Scenario/NVC12_l.TXT"
],
"Bad news, this conflict could degenerate into an open conflict between two superpowers using nukes!": [
"Scenario/IND_04_i.txt"
],
"Be advised that an American Task Force is heading towards the island. While no official declaration of war was issued, you are allowed to intervene against Americans if they pose a threat to our mission.": [
"Scenario/RED_Taipeic_i.txt"
],
"Be advised that the Chinese Navy is mobilizing its full strength to defend the island at all costs. ": [
"Scenario/RED_Taipei2i.txt",
"Scenario/RED_Taipeii.txt"
],
"Be advised that the Chinese Navy is mobilizing its full strength to defend the island at all costs. Allied forces from Japan and Australia are also converging to our aid. This is it, the final push to bring China to peace table.": [
"Scenario/RED_Taipei2i.txt"
],
"Be advised that the allies are concentrating all of their armored forces near Teagu, in preparation of a major counter-offensive. Use any means at your disposal to destroy them.": [
"Scenario/RED_Pusanci.txt"
],
"Bejing thinks we can take advantage of the two-day ceasefire announced for the Tet by striking now while the enemy is celebrating the holiday.  They should be in no position to quickly respond.": [
"Scenario/NVC08_i.txt"
],
"Bejing wants to celebrate your victory by moving your troops to a quiet place to give you and your men a rest.": [
"Scenario/NVC04_bv.TXT"
],
"Bought an RAH-66.  I hope it pulls its weight.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"But I was wrong.  Your loss, though in a sense hardly your fault, was one that was completely devastating to our cause.  ": [
"Scenario/nspegu27l.TXT"
],
"By turn 6, I was able to bring my artillery to bear on the final objectives in the north-east.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
