"Notes: Works with orginal PeG, so every version should run it.": [
"Userscen/Readme.txt"
],
"Now that the main rebellion source has vanished, Vietnam will live now in prosperity thanks to the wise words of the 'Little Red Book' and your divine 'police order' skills!": [
"Scenario/NVC12_bv.TXT"
],
"Now the putsch has failed allowing peace and order to be restored in Bangladesh.": [
"Scenario/IND4bv.TXT"
],
"Now we are forced to leave the country under the protest of UN and very likely a military intervention of USA.": [
"Scenario/NVC12_l.TXT"
],
"Now we can sit at the peace table among UN after we leave a puppet regime in Vietnam...": [
"Scenario/NVC11_bv.TXT"
],
"Of course our treaty with Bangladesh forces us to intervene to defend the oppressed population...": [
"Scenario/IND_00_i.txt"
],
"On turn 1, I expended all of my air mission points to destroy two long range enemy ADs and bring one down to 1 point.  That would, in theory, free up my Mirage 6000 to dominate the air.  But I don't have any strike aircraft, so I don't really know what good it will do me.  I suspect that I should have bought some British Harriers when I had time.  Or perhaps one of those nice little RAH-66s.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"One VH is hidden, discover it then use heliported infantry to capture the Pakistani HQ hidden in the mountains!": [
"Scenario/IND_01_i.txt"
],
"Originally we did not intend to capture the whole country but Hainoi still hopes for an external intervention of USA, this cannot happen in any way!": [
"Scenario/NVC11_i.txt"
],
"Our successful offensive in Bangladesh must be stopped since Pakistan attacked Punjab in order to avoid the collapse of the rebellion of the puppet regime in Bangladesh.": [
"Scenario/IND_01_i.txt"
],
"Pakistan has decided to neglect the peace agreements after the 1971 war who lead to the creation of Bengladesh in order to reunite the country.": [
"Scenario/IND_00_i.txt"
],
"Pakistan intervened by force in Bangladesh taking pretext of economical difficulties and existence of pro-Pakistani groups willing to overthrow the Bengladesh regime in order to reunite the country.": [
"Scenario/IND.txt"
],
"Pakistan took pretext of economical difficulties and existence of pro-Pakistani groups willing to overthrow the Bangladesh regime...": [
"Scenario/IND_00_i.txt"
],
"Sensing an opportunity, Vietnam tries to conquer South-East Asia.": [
"Scenario/RED_viet.txt"
],
"Taking advantage of WW3 in Europe and absence of possible intervention of USA and Russia, China invades Vietnam in order control its non accomodating neighbour.": [
"Scenario/NVC.txt"
],
"Thailand intervened by fear we cross its borders definitely.": [
"Scenario/NVC05_i.txt"
],
"The 155 Mk 3 picked up a leader on the first or second turn resulting in multiple fire support and devastating fire.  This will be a good unit to have.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The French and German Tigre/Tiger helicopters showed themselves to be much less capable than their American counterparts.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The Leopard 2A5 and the Challenger 3s dominated the battlefield.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The Myanmar regime keeps on protesting at the UN assembly about the violation of its territory and it is indeed wiser to leave if we do not want to wage a war against India.": [
"Scenario/NVC12_bv.TXT"
],
"The Pakistani ambassador left a note by which his country considers the conditions which led to the creation of Bangladesh in 1971 are not existing anymore but considers our peace agreement is still valid provided India does not intervene.": [
"Scenario/IND.txt"
],
"The People’s Republic of China has sued for peace, offering substantial concessions in order to avoid the embarrassment of an invasion of China, including complete independence for Taiwan and a demilitarized region in Manciuria. Celebrations erupted around the world as newscasts of the surrendering Chinese army spread. It seems your next tour will be the parade of a hero who liberated a continent.": [
"Scenario/Taipei1v.txt"
],
"The People’s Republic of China has sued for peace, offering substantial concessions in order to avoid the embarrassment of an invasion of China, including complete independence for Taiwan. Celebrations erupted the world over as newscasts of the surrendering Chinese army spread. It seems your next tour will be the parade of a hero who liberated a continent.": [
"Scenario/ns4euro18v.txt",
"Scenario/RED_Taipei1v.txt"
],
"The People’s Republic of China's invasion of South Korea under the thin guise of liberating the peninsula demands that we take swift and decisive action. Your objectives are simple: crush the North Koreans and their Chinese allies.": [
"Scenario/PUSAN3.TXT"
],
"The Russian President is outraged at your dismal performance, stating that only misguided arrogance would demand entrusting the liberation of his country to a foreign commander. The Security Council can hardly argue after the loss of men and equipment you suffered, and they have approved General Yuri Yakovlev as your replacement for the remainder of the operations in the Russian Far East. The transfer of command is effective immediately.": [
"Scenario/Khabarovskrrl.txt"
],
"The Russian government has sued for peace and opposes us no longer.": [
"Scenario/RED_Chircv.txt",
"Scenario/Volgograd2v.TXT"
],
"The U.N. did not invest its resources expecting you to fail. You will be relieved of command before you cause irreparable damage to the Coalition, though it may already be too late.": [
"Scenario/Ekaterinburgrl.txt"
],
"The Vietnamese Army has been kicked out of Laos. This is the opportunity to liberate the country...": [
"Scenario/NVC09_bv.TXT"
],
"The advance thus far has been devastating, with three-quarters proceeding up the left flank and the Australian contingent of auxiliaries and a few of my troops heading up the right flank.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The artillery did a good job.  I could have used another AVLB.  The tanks did okay, but had very few overrun attacks.  The Mirage 6000 shot up a few helos and a unit of tanks at long ranges.  But the star of the show was the battalion of Eurosams that weakened every air attack thrown at my ground units and killed a helo.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The attack of our homeland goes beyond the non respect of a peace treaty, we have called for the support of the United Nations.": [
"Scenario/IND_01_i.txt"
],
"The complete loss you suffered in Thailand has forced us to abandon all plans for a ground offensive in Indochina. You gave China the opportunity to tighten its grip on Southeast Asia, and robbed us of the ability to mount any serious challenge. Your service as a commander is no longer required.": [
"Scenario/Bangkok1l.TXT"
],
"The conflict lead to the usage of nukes by China and Russia, the world is now a huge graveyard and you are not there to see this...": [
"Scenario/IND4l.TXT"
],
"The dilema here is that the VHs are scattered in 3 different directions.  I really only have two different battlegroupds, and too few units to cover any captured hexes, so what to do?  Anyway, the Leopard 2A5 and the Challenger 3 led one group respectively, and I pretty much fashioned an infantry group to go up the west axis.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The former Republic of Taiwan surrendered at our mercy. Their former government is even now taken to a reeducation camp. ": [
"Scenario/RED_Taipeicv.txt"
],
"The government and the high command at Bejing want to congratulate you on this great victory!": [
"Scenario/NVC02_bv.TXT"
],
"The government of Russia asked as to help them regain their occupied european territories. As you are our most gifted general the president named you commander in chief of the allied forces on the European front. ": [
"Scenario/Chir1i.txt"
],
"The magnitude of your loss is immense. The People’s Republic of China has gained the upper hand in the Russian Far East. It will be some time before we can regroup for another assault. You will be serving stateside when that happens.": [
"Scenario/SAKHALIN1l.TXT"
],
"The peace agreements after the 1971 war led to the creation of Bengladesh are now clearly broken unilateraly. Of course our treaty with Bengladesh forces us to intervene to defend the oppressed population...": [
"Scenario/IND.txt"
],
"The plotters have fled to Myanmar, with a small detachment of CORE forces your order are to help the Myanmar troops to get rid of this pleague once and for all!": [
"Scenario/IND_05_i.txt"
],
"The presence of Chinese regular troops in Pakistan changes completely the situation, we can hardly continue this war alone otherwise a victory in Pakistan is impossible and worse a second invasion in India might become real and even successful!": [
"Scenario/IND3tv.TXT"
],
"The presence of Chinese troops was a nasty surprise, the sitution has became suddenly more complex from a political standpoint...": [
"Scenario/IND3bv.TXT"
],
"The sad note so far has been losing a 15 strenght Eurosam with a leader special on turn 2, but not after it shot 11 strength points out of a terrifically surprised WZ-9 helo.  RIP.": [
"Scenario/ns4PlayNotes.txt"
],
"The vacations are over, commander. Our spies in Hainoi have sent us information about an imminent enemy offensive of considerable size. It will be against our positions near Cu-Chi. Deploy your units quickly and take defensive positions first before our counterattacking.": [
"Scenario/NVC04_i.txt"
],
