],
"Your defeat at Don is a disaster of unthinkable magnitude, matched only by the mistake of entrusting you with command. Our positions throughout Russia are now threatened with collapse as their idolatrous cries for the defense of ‘Mother Russia’ have inspired fanatic attacks against our forces in the Urals. Many have been successful. You are forthwith relieved of duty.": [
"Scenario/RED_Chircl.txt"
],
"Your defeat in our bid to liberate the Malay Peninsula is an absolute catastrophe. The media is all over this fiasco with dire predictions of the losses in both men and equipment that a protracted war in Southeast Asia is bound to cost. Faced with intensely negative public opinion, the President thinks it prudent to cut our losses before they become unconscionable. His first order is to remove you from command.": [
"Scenario/Singapore1l.TXT"
],
"Your success in Southeast Asia was a spectacular feat, more so since the Russian offensive was an absolute failure. Their government has demanded that you personally lead the liberation of the Soviet Far East. Apparently, your name has obtained legendary status among the Russian people. The Joint Chiefs agree. Maintaining pressure on Chinese forces in Siberia is essential as our navy looks for an opening on the Chinese coast.": [
"Scenario/ALMATY1I.TXT"
],
